WEBVTT

00:01.310 --> 00:03.160
<i>When we were in elementary school,</i>

00:02.320 --> 00:04.800
I always fail at the jump...

00:03.160 --> 00:07.040
<i>Tomoko was popular, and I was a nuisance.</i>

00:08.020 --> 00:11.990
<i>Tomoko was the mood-maker type 
who built everyone up,</i>

00:11.990 --> 00:13.960
<i>and I was the complete opposite.</i>

00:13.960 --> 00:15.730
<i>Shy and awkward with words,</i>

00:15.730 --> 00:17.500
<i>I set everyone around me on edge.</i>

00:19.400 --> 00:20.500
<i>Maybe that was why,</i>

00:21.000 --> 00:23.400
<i>in the beginning, I hated Tomoko's guts.</i>

00:26.440 --> 00:28.680
<i>Everyone has their own circumstances.</i>

00:28.680 --> 00:31.620
<i>I was what people refer 
to as a neglected child.</i>

00:31.980 --> 00:36.150
<i>Whenever my mom was cozying up 
to a prospective new husband,</i>

00:36.150 --> 00:39.020
<i>I would find myself locked out of the house.</i>

00:39.370 --> 00:42.930
<i>In the beginning, I just had to kill 
a little time when this happened,</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:46.880
<i>but at some point, I started 
spending most of the day outside.</i>

00:47.470 --> 00:50.440
<i>While the sun was up, I had playmates.</i>

00:50.440 --> 00:52.030
<i>It was the nights that were painful.</i>

00:54.030 --> 00:55.310
<i>That's why...</i>

00:56.040 --> 01:00.040
<i>I'd spend time at a friend's house 
and get treated to a meal.</i>

01:00.600 --> 01:03.540
<i>Each household welcomed me cheerfully.</i>

01:04.110 --> 01:06.050
<i>In the beginning, at least.</i>

01:08.260 --> 01:10.050
<i>Yes? Who is it?</i>

01:10.050 --> 01:12.310
<i>It's me. I came to hang out.</i>

01:12.310 --> 01:15.380
Oh, Shizuku-chan. Hold on a minute.

01:16.040 --> 01:18.680
Mama, Shizuku-chan is here!

01:18.680 --> 01:22.060
She's here again? What kind of 
manners are they teaching her?

01:22.060 --> 01:24.600
<i>And she always stays for dinner. 
She's shameless.</i>

01:24.600 --> 01:26.440
<i>I told you not to invite her anymore.</i>

01:26.440 --> 01:29.130
<i>I didn't invite her. We're not even friends.</i>

01:29.130 --> 01:31.950
<i>Really? Then I'll send her home.</i>

01:32.380 --> 01:36.000
<i>Shizuku-chan? We have other plans 
today, so we can't invite you in.</i>

01:36.000 --> 01:37.430
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

01:37.950 --> 01:39.220
Shizuku-chan?

01:39.620 --> 01:42.210
What? There's no one there.

01:44.890 --> 01:48.360
<i>My classmates started avoiding me.</i>

01:48.960 --> 01:52.970
<i>I figured it was better that way, since 
they wouldn't find out about my situation.</i>

02:08.570 --> 02:13.360
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:08.570 --> 02:13.360
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

03:34.770 --> 03:39.910
<b>A Station, Scissors, and a Haircut</b>

03:34.770 --> 03:39.910
<b>A Station, Scissors, and a Haircut</b>

03:41.330 --> 03:42.990
<i>Listen to me, Oto-chan.</i>

03:42.990 --> 03:44.940
<i>Do not answer that door!</i>

03:44.940 --> 03:46.870
<i>Get out of the building immediately!</i>

03:47.160 --> 03:48.460
Shizuku-san!

03:58.750 --> 04:00.140
Not that way!

04:00.140 --> 04:01.140
Come on!

04:01.140 --> 04:02.540
Apartment wife!

04:07.710 --> 04:08.920
What is all this?

04:08.920 --> 04:10.020
Let's go!

04:21.030 --> 04:22.490
The shutters!

04:23.530 --> 04:26.090
They were open when I came in a moment ago!

04:26.090 --> 04:27.730
What do we do, apartment wife?

04:27.730 --> 04:29.550
Crap. We have to go back!

04:32.370 --> 04:34.540
That should hold for a little while.

04:35.030 --> 04:36.980
So, mind explaining?

04:37.580 --> 04:39.800
What the hell is going on here?

04:40.700 --> 04:44.810
The hong yi xiao nu hai attacks 
whoever answers its knocking.

04:46.870 --> 04:50.190
Oto-chan has already answered it once.

04:50.190 --> 04:52.080
That's why she was targeted.

04:52.080 --> 04:55.060
No, that's not what I'm asking!

04:55.060 --> 04:57.940
What do you mean, it's Tomoko herself?

04:57.940 --> 05:02.200
The current hong yi xiao nu hai 
is a chimera of several Curiosities.

05:02.200 --> 05:05.950
Originally, it was a Curiosity that simply 
took people into the mountains,

05:06.350 --> 05:08.050
but as the story was told,

05:08.050 --> 05:12.210
it combined with one of a ghost that haunts 
and kills those who answer its knocking.

05:12.210 --> 05:17.490
It also got mixed with tales of the shui gui,
which drown those who approach water,

05:17.490 --> 05:19.210
adding the element of rain.

05:19.960 --> 05:24.650
Finally, the shui gui has one more 
characteristic we can't afford to ignore.

05:25.240 --> 05:27.460
"Ti si gui."

05:25.510 --> 05:27.470
<b>\h\h\hTi Si Gui\h\h\h
(Death Swap)</b>

05:27.870 --> 05:32.900
When a shui gui leads a human to its death, 
that shui gui can then leave this world,

05:32.900 --> 05:38.490
but the murdered human then becomes 
a new shui gui looking for a fresh victim.

05:39.250 --> 05:42.640
This special swapping characteristic, 
called ti si gui,

05:42.640 --> 05:44.990
is passed down in folklore 
across the continent.

05:45.540 --> 05:48.870
It's similar to the shichinin misaki in Japan.

05:49.370 --> 05:51.370
<i>The shichinin misaki?</i>

05:49.460 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.460 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.510 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.510 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.510 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.520 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.650 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.670 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.820 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.840 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.880 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:49.930 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:50.000 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:50.020 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:50.030 --> 05:51.370
<b>Shichinin Misaki</b>

05:51.370 --> 05:55.420
Yes. A group of seven vengeful 
ghosts who always act together.

05:55.420 --> 05:58.850
When someone encounters them, 
they are killed and join their ranks,

05:58.850 --> 06:00.880
at which point the oldest one can leave.

06:01.440 --> 06:05.130
After these stories and the hong yi 
xiao nu hai were brought together,

06:05.130 --> 06:08.620
the result was a story about someone who 
goes out on rainy nights to knock on doors,

06:08.620 --> 06:10.020
trying to get someone to open them.

06:10.020 --> 06:12.600
It became a wandering Curiosity.

06:14.520 --> 06:16.270
Just give it to me straight.

06:16.270 --> 06:18.270
Is Tomoko still alive?

06:20.670 --> 06:23.780
No. Tomoko-san is already dead.

06:24.500 --> 06:25.820
Why?

06:26.280 --> 06:28.380
Why? Why?

06:28.670 --> 06:32.090
Tomoko-san is alive! 
They're going to see each other again!

06:32.090 --> 06:33.110
Oto-chan...

06:33.110 --> 06:37.060
Shizuku-san! They got it wrong! 
There must be some mistake!

06:37.360 --> 06:39.190
I'm going to go get changed.

06:39.190 --> 06:41.980
I just can't relax in this outfit.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.170
Shizuku-san?

06:45.050 --> 06:48.200
Leave the door open! If you don't...

06:48.200 --> 06:49.560
I know.

06:50.270 --> 06:51.940
Sorry for all the trouble.

06:53.060 --> 06:54.220
Thank you.

06:55.390 --> 06:56.370
Shizuku-san!

06:56.370 --> 06:57.940
What is she thinking?!

06:58.420 --> 06:59.940
Why?

07:03.070 --> 07:05.580
I made my peace with this a long time ago.

07:06.160 --> 07:10.450
The details just ended up being a lot 
worse than I expected. That's all.

07:10.450 --> 07:14.140
Still, if it means I can see her again, 
it beats the alternative.

07:17.760 --> 07:19.460
It's been a while, Tomoko.

07:20.900 --> 07:22.410
Do you remember?

07:23.230 --> 07:27.100
Back then, you were the one 
who opened the door for me.

07:34.130 --> 07:35.730
Shizuku-chan?

07:49.240 --> 07:50.450
Here.

08:09.770 --> 08:13.260
It wasn't anything special, 
just normal thoughtfulness, right?

08:13.740 --> 08:15.580
Because you're a kind person.

08:16.540 --> 08:20.150
For you, I was just one friend among many.

08:20.150 --> 08:26.370
But for me, you were the one person 
in the whole world I could call my friend.

08:27.020 --> 08:29.990
That's not true. There are 
the others at the café, right?

08:29.990 --> 08:32.410
And there's me! There's me, too!

08:33.280 --> 08:35.920
You're a kind person, too, Adashino Oto.

08:36.330 --> 08:39.380
But back then, I made up my mind.

08:39.730 --> 08:44.430
I told myself that I'd give the rest of my life 
for Tomoko, just for this one moment.

08:47.600 --> 08:49.970
I was happy to be able to live with you.

08:50.450 --> 08:53.340
Congrats on having your dream 
of becoming a beautician come true.

08:54.080 --> 08:55.990
I was always cheering for you, you know?

08:56.730 --> 08:59.360
Even though we haven't really 
been able to talk lately.

09:00.440 --> 09:02.240
Shizuku-san, don't do it!

09:02.240 --> 09:03.230
Move!

09:07.820 --> 09:10.320
Thank you, Adashino Oto.

09:10.320 --> 09:12.570
Thanks to you, I'm able to grieve.

09:14.840 --> 09:17.330
Shizuku-san, please stop!

10:06.000 --> 10:07.140
Tomoko.

10:07.890 --> 10:10.190
I've been looking for you.

10:10.190 --> 10:14.150
But I wasn't able to find you. I'm sorry.

10:24.560 --> 10:26.860
I will set you free.

10:33.080 --> 10:34.240
Shizuku-san?

10:38.880 --> 10:40.240
I saw her.

10:51.470 --> 10:54.910
Adashino Oto, I...

11:00.510 --> 11:02.260
Shizuku-san?

11:19.220 --> 11:23.830
It's too cruel. This isn't right.

11:25.180 --> 11:26.790
<i>Ren-nii!</i>

11:30.770 --> 11:33.050
<i>Leave it to me, Oto.</i>

11:33.050 --> 11:34.280
Ren-nii!

11:34.800 --> 11:36.130
I have to stop him!

11:37.040 --> 11:39.090
Ren-nii is going to use his Eyes!

11:44.000 --> 11:45.310
Shizuku-san!

11:45.710 --> 11:47.530
Ren-nii, your Eyes...

11:47.530 --> 11:50.080
Eyes? I haven't used them.

11:51.140 --> 11:52.820
I used this.

11:53.370 --> 11:55.190
A test sheet?

11:55.190 --> 11:58.500
What do you think? I'm very proud 
of this treasure of mine!

11:58.500 --> 11:59.800
That's mine, though.

11:59.800 --> 12:02.080
This makes no sense. Explain.

12:02.630 --> 12:04.130
There's an ancient Curiosity overseas

12:04.130 --> 12:07.080
called the mo-sin-a that carries 
people into the mountains.

12:05.120 --> 12:07.080
<b>\h\h\hMo-Sin-A\h\h\h
(Demon Child)</b>

12:07.710 --> 12:11.220
There are tales of its eyes, clothes, 
or hat being red. It's a childlike Curiosity.

12:11.760 --> 12:15.710
The other key I found was a ghost 
story that's popular in Japan.

12:16.380 --> 12:20.840
When you think of a childlike Curiosity 
wearing red in Japan, what comes to mind?

12:22.460 --> 12:24.230
Toilet-bound Hanako-san?

12:24.600 --> 12:26.320
Exactly.

12:26.900 --> 12:31.530
It's likely that a combination 
of the mo-sin-a and Hanako-san

12:31.530 --> 12:33.610
resulted in the hong yi xiao nu hai.

12:34.000 --> 12:37.830
So I used the characteristics of the 
combined Curiosity to my advantage.

12:38.200 --> 12:40.710
"Show her a test sheet 
with a score of one hundred."

12:41.730 --> 12:44.120
It's a famous method to drive Hanako-san away.

12:44.120 --> 12:46.370
I'm amazed you had something like that ready.

12:46.710 --> 12:50.260
I have all of Oto's test papers 
carefully preserved!

12:51.240 --> 12:55.010
I am forever perplexed by your staggering 
over-fondness as an older brother.

12:55.010 --> 12:57.300
Then Shizuku-san is safe?

12:57.300 --> 12:58.770
No, not yet.

12:58.770 --> 13:01.000
The Curiosity has only 
temporarily been held at bay.

13:02.900 --> 13:04.390
Let's head to the station.

13:04.760 --> 13:07.520
<b>KISARAGI</b>

13:06.770 --> 13:08.950
I'm so sorry, Sumireko-san.

13:08.950 --> 13:11.590
If I weren't still recovering, I'd help you.

13:11.990 --> 13:14.870
You really are an infuriating kid.

13:15.520 --> 13:17.300
Thank you for your hard work.

13:17.700 --> 13:20.750
I'll go and get a ticket. 
If you'll wait here, please?

13:20.750 --> 13:23.260
A ticket? What are you planning to do?

13:23.260 --> 13:24.780
No, wait, before that...

13:24.780 --> 13:26.790
Is this Kisaragi Station?

13:29.550 --> 13:32.790
Isn't it about time you showed me your hand?

13:33.140 --> 13:37.760
If you're asking if this is the mysterious 
station that appears in urban legends,

13:38.670 --> 13:39.670
then yes.

13:39.670 --> 13:42.080
I knew it! This is Kisaragi Station!

13:42.080 --> 13:46.000
The otherworldly station that exists 
in both this world and another!

13:46.000 --> 13:48.760
I'm inside that urban legend right now!

13:50.020 --> 13:53.060
More importantly, we need 
to finish the business at hand.

13:53.350 --> 13:56.820
Sumireko-san, you picked something 
up in that building, didn't you?

13:57.960 --> 14:01.330
You mean these scissors? 
Shizuku-san was holding them.

14:06.530 --> 14:08.090
I knew it.

14:08.090 --> 14:09.960
They're a cursed object.

14:10.630 --> 14:14.850
<i>If you are here to report a found item, 
please come this way.</i>

14:16.660 --> 14:20.420
<i>It's quite lively here today, 
mysterious disappearances.</i>

14:20.960 --> 14:24.310
<i>Oh, and a Bearer of Youth. How unusual.</i>

14:24.310 --> 14:27.900
<i>Will you be exchanging 
that woman for a ticket?</i>

14:30.620 --> 14:32.980
<i>I have no intention of 
turning over a friend to you.</i>

14:32.980 --> 14:37.610
<i>My apologies. Then what 
will you be exchanging today?</i>

14:49.560 --> 14:50.550
<i>This.</i>

14:50.550 --> 14:53.760
<i>A newly formed cursed object, is it?</i>

14:53.760 --> 14:56.300
<i>But it doesn't appear to be a pure one.</i>

14:56.300 --> 14:59.880
<i>It won't take you as far as 
your desired destination.</i>

14:59.880 --> 15:02.630
<i>However far it will go is fine.</i>

15:03.170 --> 15:06.380
<i>But the only one riding the train 
will be the hong yi xiao nu hai.</i>

15:08.610 --> 15:12.370
The train will be here soon. 
Head straight to the platform.

15:12.370 --> 15:14.220
Yes, I understand.

15:22.650 --> 15:25.150
<b>Express</b>

15:22.650 --> 15:25.150
<b>Train Approaching</b>

15:35.260 --> 15:36.840
Adashino Oto?

15:36.840 --> 15:38.180
Shizuku-san!

15:38.670 --> 15:41.320
I'm not dead?

15:41.320 --> 15:43.530
Did I mess it up?

15:43.530 --> 15:45.040
Calm down.

15:45.040 --> 15:50.250
Shizuku-san, the hong yi xiao nu hai 
possessed you, and you disappeared.

15:50.250 --> 15:52.680
But then my brother stopped it.

15:53.510 --> 15:56.510
This station is a Curiosity 
that connects to another world.

15:56.510 --> 15:58.690
The train will be here in ten minutes.

15:59.900 --> 16:03.330
If we can make sure only the 
hong yi xiao nu hai gets on the train,

16:03.330 --> 16:04.540
you'll be safe.

16:05.010 --> 16:06.450
I see.

16:06.800 --> 16:09.780
Then I was able to draw the Curiosity to me.

16:10.550 --> 16:14.340
In that case, everything's 
all right, Adashino Oto.

16:15.200 --> 16:21.000
You know, when I was investigating 
Tomoko-san, I talked to all kinds of people.

16:21.000 --> 16:24.550
I asked them what they knew 
about Tomoko-san's friends.

16:25.060 --> 16:27.760
They all told me the same thing.

16:27.760 --> 16:29.890
"She went shopping with Shizuku."

16:29.890 --> 16:32.490
"She went out to eat with Shizuku."

16:32.490 --> 16:37.390
"Tomoko-chan was always talking about 
the things she did with a girl named Shizuku."

16:37.770 --> 16:43.230
Do you still think that, to Tomoko-san, 
you were just one friend among many?

16:44.250 --> 16:48.360
And it's because Tomoko-san 
left you her scissors

16:48.360 --> 16:50.810
that we were able to get this train ticket.

17:02.690 --> 17:07.190
I'm certain that Tomoko-san 
wants you to live.

17:08.600 --> 17:11.760
<i>The train... arriving shortly.</i>

17:11.760 --> 17:16.260
<i>For your safety... behind... line.</i>

17:19.170 --> 17:21.560
It's just about time for the train to arrive.

17:21.980 --> 17:25.270
Was it all right to send Oto-chan on her own?

17:25.270 --> 17:27.390
She'll be fine.

17:27.390 --> 17:29.590
She's far more grounded than she appears.

17:30.100 --> 17:33.680
I'd be much more worried if I had 
to leave you here on your own.

17:33.680 --> 17:35.600
Your concern is unnecessary.

17:35.600 --> 17:38.090
At least, that's what I'd like to say.

17:38.090 --> 17:39.750
To be honest, I'm glad you're here.

17:40.570 --> 17:43.920
This place freaks me out 
more than I thought it would.

17:47.340 --> 17:51.220
That voice from the ticket window... 
I couldn't understand what it was saying,

17:51.860 --> 17:54.970
but I could tell it was something humans shouldn't get involved with.

17:54.970 --> 17:58.610
There are some things we're better off 
living our lives without knowing, if possible.

17:58.610 --> 18:01.680
That's why you deliberately 
didn't tell me anything, right?

18:01.680 --> 18:04.570
You're speaking too highly of me.

18:04.980 --> 18:07.690
I was just too scared to talk about it.

18:14.410 --> 18:19.200
Why is the train packed at this 
time of day? Who are these people?

18:31.250 --> 18:34.560
Cursed objects and Curiosities 
are foreign to this world.

18:35.040 --> 18:38.220
They are impurities that don't belong here.

18:48.760 --> 18:55.200
And the world is always desperate 
to rid itself of such foreign objects.

19:01.380 --> 19:05.460
So this station was brought into existence 
in order to expel these unneeded

19:05.460 --> 19:07.370
foreign bodies from this world.

19:21.760 --> 19:23.640
Cursed objects serve as the fare.

19:24.180 --> 19:27.620
And our home is at the very end of this line.

19:28.390 --> 19:31.890
That's why we're looking for cursed objects 
that can take us all the way there.

19:32.700 --> 19:34.500
To stay alive and return home...

19:35.110 --> 19:37.560
That's our goal as siblings.

19:40.260 --> 19:42.850
We're castaways from another world.

19:47.920 --> 19:51.010
So you finally fessed up, huh?

19:51.010 --> 19:53.800
Did you think I'd get 
creeped out if you told me?

19:53.800 --> 19:58.290
If I'm being honest, thanks to 
the events of these last few weeks,

19:58.290 --> 20:02.080
I'm overflowing with more creativity 
than I have been in a long while.

20:02.080 --> 20:05.060
I'm not gonna let you two do 
all the fun stuff on your own!

20:06.000 --> 20:07.310
Sumireko-san...

20:07.970 --> 20:12.200
Besides, you promised to read 
my next work, didn't you?

20:12.200 --> 20:13.570
I'm not letting you back out now.

20:16.250 --> 20:19.030
That's definitely the move of 
a meddling, mature woman.

20:20.610 --> 20:23.980
You're both all right? 
What about the hong yi xiao nu hai?

20:23.980 --> 20:24.950
We sent it off.

20:24.950 --> 20:28.710
I'm sorry. You've done so much 
for me, Ogawa-no-neesan.

20:28.710 --> 20:32.090
"Neesan"? Well, that's laudable of you.

20:32.500 --> 20:35.440
I felt like I should live 
enough for Tomoko, too.

20:35.440 --> 20:37.530
Thanks, Occhan!

20:37.920 --> 20:40.770
And where is this older brother of yours?

20:40.770 --> 20:42.720
At least let me say thanks!

20:43.420 --> 20:46.470
Huh? Maybe he stepped outside earlier?

20:49.230 --> 20:50.580
Let's go and see.

21:04.440 --> 21:06.490
<i>You're certainly working yourself to the bone.</i>

21:06.910 --> 21:10.470
<i>You're not her brother by blood, 
to say nothing of not even being human.</i>

21:10.470 --> 21:13.750
<i>You're just a sham of a monster.</i>

21:16.250 --> 21:18.980
<i>How many years has it been since you slept?</i>

21:19.700 --> 21:22.770
<i>Do you remember the last time you ate?</i>

21:22.770 --> 21:27.100
<i>Has there been even the briefest moment 
in which your suffering has eased?</i>

21:29.940 --> 21:34.770
<i>Soon, you'll be worn down to nothing 
for your sister's sake and disappear.</i>

21:35.590 --> 21:41.370
<i>Whether you have a ticket or not, 
there is no station to which you can return.</i>

21:46.810 --> 21:49.190
<i>Even so, that girl deserves to go home.</i>

21:50.330 --> 21:53.200
<i>Oto really is just a lost child.</i>

21:53.630 --> 21:55.900
<i>There are people waiting for her, 
looking for her.</i>

21:57.010 --> 22:02.660
<i>I'm going to prove that she isn't 
someone that no one needs.</i>

